# Project rules — follow to avoid regressions

## Renaming (TS/JS)
- When renaming an exported or returned symbol (e.g. hook return key, prop name):
  1. Rename the **definition** in the same file (e.g. internal variable).
  2. Keep **return/export** keys and variable names in sync (object shorthand uses variable name).
  3. Update **all call sites** (consumers, types, props).
- After a rename: search the repo for both the **old** and **new** name; fix any leftover old name in the same role.

## CSS
- Every rule must have: **selector** `{` **properties** `}`. No orphan `}` and no rule that is only `Selector {` with no body and no closing `}`.
- After editing a .css file: verify brace balance and that no block is missing selector or closing brace.

## Before finishing edits
- If you changed frontend code: ensure the app builds or runs (e.g. `npm run build` or dev server) so CSS and runtime errors are caught.

See docs/EDITING_DISCIPLINE.md for full checklist.
